### to_array'

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"inl to_array' forall dim t. (items : seq' t) : a dim t =\n    backend_switch {\n        Gleam = fun () =>\n            global \"import gary/array\"\n            $'!items |> array.from_list' : a dim t\n        Fsharp = fun () => items |> $'Seq.toArray' : a dim t\n        // A numpy object array (listm'.to_array'): `np` is not bound in Python output and CuPy holds primitives only.\n        Python = fun () =>\n            inl x = ($'!items ' : listm'.list' t) |> listm'.to_array'\n            $'!x ' : a dim t\n        Rust = fun () => $'Rc::new(RefCell::new((*!items).clone()))' : a dim t\n        TypeScript = fun () => $'[...!items]' : a dim t\n    }","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl to_array' forall dim t. (items : seq' t) : a dim t =
      backend_switch {
          Gleam = fun () =>
              global "import gary/array"
              $'!items |> array.from_list' : a dim t
          Fsharp = fun () => items |> $'Seq.toArray' : a dim t
          // A numpy object array (listm'.to_array'): `np` is not bound in Python output and CuPy holds primitives only.
          Python = fun () =>
              inl x = ($'!items ' : listm'.list' t) |> listm'.to_array'
              $'!x ' : a dim t
          Rust = fun () => $'Rc::new(RefCell::new((*!items).clone()))' : a dim t
          TypeScript = fun () => $'[...!items]' : a dim t
      }
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

